WEBVTT

00:01.080 --> 00:02.957
Okay, okay, okay.
It's your birthday.

00:03.120 --> 00:05.395
We're going to a ball game,
only got three tickets.

00:05.560 --> 00:07.073
- Cool.
- It's not his birthday.

00:07.240 --> 00:09.151
- What else you get me?
- Not your birthday.

00:09.320 --> 00:11.914
- Charlie, what's going on?
- I've got a delicate situation.

00:12.080 --> 00:15.311
- I need to appear as if I have plans.
- Does your situation have a name?

00:15.480 --> 00:18.040
I'm sure she does.
Just follow my lead.

00:18.200 --> 00:19.997
- Dodgers or Angels?
- Let's say Dodgers.

00:20.160 --> 00:22.230
See, the kid knows how to do this.

00:22.880 --> 00:25.599
I'll get my mitt. Oh, boy, a ball game.

00:26.520 --> 00:28.795
- Now, that's commitment.
- That's not commitment.

00:28.960 --> 00:30.518
That's lead paint in the nursery.

00:30.680 --> 00:33.399
Hey, Steve, you down there?

00:33.560 --> 00:35.630
Oh, yeah, and my name's Steve.

00:36.480 --> 00:37.469
Coming.

00:37.640 --> 00:40.757
Charlie, I'm not gonna lie to some
poor woman so you can dump her.

00:40.920 --> 00:42.751
I am not dumping her.

00:42.920 --> 00:44.638
We've just grown apart.

00:44.800 --> 00:47.189
Since you picked her up
at a bar last night?

00:47.720 --> 00:48.914
People change.

00:50.560 --> 00:51.549
Hello?

00:51.720 --> 00:53.472
Oh, God.

00:54.680 --> 00:55.669
In here, Mom.

00:55.840 --> 00:58.274
So, what are my boys up to today?

01:01.240 --> 01:04.277
We're going to a Dodger game,
and we've only got three tickets.

01:12.640 --> 01:15.757
So you're on your way to a ball game.

01:15.920 --> 01:18.115
Yep. It's a little treat
for Jake's birthday.

01:18.280 --> 01:19.759
That was months ago.

01:21.360 --> 01:23.954
We were waiting for bobblehead day.

01:26.000 --> 01:29.356
It's good for Jake
to see other bobbleheads.

01:30.680 --> 01:32.079
Hey, Dad, I just checked online.

01:32.240 --> 01:34.834
The Dodgers are in San Francisco today.

01:36.440 --> 01:39.432
Yes, well, we'd better get going then.

01:42.160 --> 01:43.912
It's quite a drive.

01:44.080 --> 01:47.152
Must you continue
with this pathetic, little charade?

01:47.600 --> 01:49.955
At this point, we're kind of committed.

01:50.640 --> 01:52.551
All right, we're not going to a ball game.

01:52.720 --> 01:55.553
We're not?
Man, this is the worst birthday ever.

01:55.720 --> 01:58.359
Why do you have to lie to me?

01:58.520 --> 02:00.397
We don't have to.
It's a choice we make.

02:01.200 --> 02:03.998
Well, you both might find this
all amusing.

02:04.160 --> 02:06.674
But I do have feelings, and I can be hurt.

02:08.080 --> 02:09.069
Sorry, Mom.

02:09.240 --> 02:12.391
It's just crushing to know
that my own sons think so little of me.

02:12.560 --> 02:14.915
Really? After all this time?

02:15.760 --> 02:16.954
Charlie.

02:17.120 --> 02:19.315
We're both sorry.
Is there anything we can do?

02:19.480 --> 02:21.152
Well, as a matter of fact there is.

02:21.320 --> 02:23.117
Oh, you just walked right into that.

02:24.200 --> 02:26.156
Teddy is out of town,
and I need an escort...

02:26.320 --> 02:28.550
...for the Civic Light Opera benefit
this evening.

02:28.720 --> 02:30.756
Why don't you try
one of those escort services?

02:30.920 --> 02:33.354
Charlie, if I were gonna pay
$200 per hour for a man...

02:33.520 --> 02:35.909
...I would not be taking him
to the opera.

02:36.080 --> 02:37.069
That's fair.

02:37.240 --> 02:40.118
Well, I'd love to help you out, Mom,
but I have a date tonight.

02:40.920 --> 02:45.471
Oh, so now it's inflatable-sex-doll night
at Dodger Stadium.

02:46.440 --> 02:47.668
No.

02:47.840 --> 02:49.512
No, I really have a date.

02:49.680 --> 02:51.955
And the doll was a gag gift
from one of my patients.

02:52.720 --> 02:53.835
Charlie, what about you?

02:54.360 --> 02:56.828
I tried it once, but I prefer
a real woman.

02:57.440 --> 03:00.079
Do you have plans this evening?

03:00.240 --> 03:01.355
Oh, l... Well...

03:01.520 --> 03:03.192
Hey, Steve.

03:03.360 --> 03:05.191
In here.

03:05.360 --> 03:06.998
As a matter of fact, I do have plans.

03:07.160 --> 03:09.993
I have a very special lady friend
over for the weekend.

03:10.160 --> 03:11.991
And here she is now. Hey, baby.

03:12.160 --> 03:13.513
Hi.

03:14.760 --> 03:16.034
Excuse me.

03:21.040 --> 03:22.109
Isn't she something?

03:26.240 --> 03:28.708
Okay, but get a town car,
because I ain't going sober.

03:36.360 --> 03:37.349
Your town car's here.

03:37.920 --> 03:39.239
Terrific.

03:39.400 --> 03:40.389
Come on.

03:40.560 --> 03:44.030
I have been to these things with Mom,
and I know you think it's gonna be bad.

03:44.200 --> 03:48.079
But believe me, it's gonna be worse
than you can even imagine.

03:48.240 --> 03:50.310
You're really enjoying this, aren't you?

03:50.480 --> 03:52.516
You just love seeing me unhappy.

03:52.680 --> 03:55.433
Well, yeah.

03:56.000 --> 03:58.958
Did you feel sorry for me
when I had to wear that cowboy outfit...

03:59.120 --> 04:00.553
...to her celebrity AIDS hoedown?

04:01.280 --> 04:02.679
- That was different.
- How?

04:02.840 --> 04:04.034
It was you.

04:04.760 --> 04:07.115
Yeah, well, now it's you.

04:07.280 --> 04:09.669
Yippee kay yay, mother accompanier.

04:15.240 --> 04:16.912
Want a few tips?

04:17.080 --> 04:18.069
Like what?

04:18.240 --> 04:19.389
Well, let's see.

04:19.560 --> 04:22.120
Mom likes to starve herself
for a few days before these...

04:22.280 --> 04:23.679
...so she can fit into her gown.

04:23.840 --> 04:27.230
That means she'll be knocking back
vodka gimlets on an empty stomach.

04:27.800 --> 04:32.191
- Oh, jeez, she can be a cranky drunk.
- Cranky?

04:32.680 --> 04:35.911
I got bitch-slapped
with my own 10-gallon hat.

04:36.560 --> 04:39.552
So, what's the tip?
Don't wear a 10-gallon hat?

04:39.720 --> 04:42.632
All you have to do is bring along
a little baggie of crackers...

04:42.800 --> 04:44.233
...you know, saltines, Goldfish.

04:44.400 --> 04:47.153
Anything you can stuff down her throat
to soak up the booze.

04:47.920 --> 04:49.672
How about a throw pillow?

04:51.160 --> 04:53.958
Oh, oh, and whatever you do,
don't let her take off her shoes.

04:54.120 --> 04:55.473
- Why not?
- Well, A,

04:55.640 --> 04:57.631
...you'll be carrying them all night,
and B...

04:57.800 --> 04:59.279
...you'll wind up giving her
a foot massage.

04:59.440 --> 05:01.396
That's not something
anybody wants to see.

05:02.000 --> 05:03.115
Oh, God.

05:03.280 --> 05:06.272
Not to mention the fact
that it puts you on bunion patrol.

05:08.720 --> 05:10.358
Anyway, have fun.

05:11.120 --> 05:15.238
I'm off to pick up a beautiful, smart,
funny, sexually-available woman...

05:15.400 --> 05:18.198
...who, best of all, is not my mother.

05:18.800 --> 05:21.030
Give it time. You'll get her there.

05:22.840 --> 05:25.638
In consideration of the evening
you have ahead of you...

05:25.800 --> 05:27.472
...I'm gonna let you have that one.

05:33.080 --> 05:35.594
Yeah, these are the good times.

05:40.400 --> 05:41.515
Another gimlet, please.

05:41.680 --> 05:44.069
You sure you don't want a Wheat Thin?

05:45.880 --> 05:47.518
Wheaty.

05:47.680 --> 05:49.591
No, I need the liquor to dull the pain.

05:49.760 --> 05:51.318
My shoes are killing me.

05:51.480 --> 05:54.995
Yeah, but they look wonderful on your
feet, right where they are now.

05:55.280 --> 05:57.999
- Oh, look who's over there.
- Who?

05:58.160 --> 06:00.879
One of the most powerful
union leaders in Hollywood.

06:01.360 --> 06:02.793
What about him?

06:05.320 --> 06:07.914
- Really? The mob?
- Yeah.

06:08.080 --> 06:11.117
They say he killed a writer once
just to make a point.

06:11.760 --> 06:13.432
What was the point?

06:13.840 --> 06:15.114
"I can kill a writer."

06:17.280 --> 06:19.589
- And the silver-haired man he's talking to.
- Yeah?

06:19.760 --> 06:23.275
That is the king
of vaginal-rejuvenation surgery.

06:23.440 --> 06:26.477
But, interestingly,
he's never used one himself...

06:26.640 --> 06:28.437
...rejuvenated or otherwise.

06:30.040 --> 06:32.600
Wouldn't that make him
the queen of vaginal surgery?

06:33.520 --> 06:35.033
Good for you, Charlie.

06:35.200 --> 06:36.394
I wish I'd thought of that.

06:36.560 --> 06:37.959
And from now on, I did.

06:38.880 --> 06:39.869
It's yours.

06:40.040 --> 06:41.996
So, what other dirt you got?

06:42.160 --> 06:45.835
Oh, darling, you know,
I don't like to speak ill of anyone.

06:48.480 --> 06:49.469
All right.

06:49.640 --> 06:54.270
Bankrupt, embezzler, tushie tuck,
bigamist, pill freak.

06:54.440 --> 06:55.759
And that one over there?

06:55.920 --> 06:59.230
Underwent surgery to have a cell phone
removed from his lower intestine.

07:00.920 --> 07:03.434
- How in the world did it get there?
- One can speculate.

07:03.600 --> 07:06.194
But I have it on good authority
that it was set to vibrate.

07:08.560 --> 07:10.198
How do you know all these things?

07:10.360 --> 07:13.909
Oh, Charlie,
it's my business to know these things.

07:14.080 --> 07:19.837
High-end real estate is all about gathering
information and forging relationships.

07:20.000 --> 07:21.115
Hello, Beatrice, darling.

07:21.280 --> 07:25.239
Lovely to see you,
you two-dollar whore.

07:25.920 --> 07:28.593
You know, Mom, it's great
to watch you doing autopsies...

07:28.760 --> 07:30.034
...when I'm not the cadaver.

07:30.200 --> 07:32.475
Half the fun is sharing
with someone you love.

07:32.640 --> 07:34.437
You see that statuesque woman
over there?

07:34.600 --> 07:36.511
The one with the knock-off
Prada handbag?

07:36.680 --> 07:38.238
Don't tell me. She's not a woman.

07:38.400 --> 07:39.628
Oh, she's a woman.

07:39.800 --> 07:41.916
She's an amazing woman.

07:42.080 --> 07:44.992
She built a children's hospital
in Guatemala.

07:45.160 --> 07:46.354
Yeah, and...?

07:46.520 --> 07:50.274
Once they're healthy enough to walk,
she flies them to Los Angeles...

07:50.440 --> 07:53.034
...and leases them out to celebrities
as household slaves.

07:53.200 --> 07:54.269
Hello, dear.

07:56.600 --> 07:58.750
I'm trying to sell her home.

07:58.920 --> 08:01.878
Kind of hard to put a good spin
on media-room-slash-dungeon.

08:08.640 --> 08:10.596
I'm sorry, Alan. I can't do this.

08:10.760 --> 08:12.478
Sure you can. I mean, you are.

08:12.640 --> 08:16.189
And if you'll allow me to say so,
you're pretty good at it.

08:16.360 --> 08:17.873
It's not you, it's me.

08:18.680 --> 08:20.671
- Yeah, right.
- What is that supposed to mean?

08:20.840 --> 08:26.949
Sharon, I have been rejected
by 32 different women in my life.

08:27.120 --> 08:29.634
And you know what?
It's never been me.

08:30.360 --> 08:32.191
Okay, it's you. Feel better?

08:32.880 --> 08:34.677
Actually, no.

08:34.840 --> 08:35.909
You're a very nice guy.

08:36.080 --> 08:38.640
That's even worse. You know
what they say about nice guys.

08:38.800 --> 08:39.915
Yes, they finish last.

08:40.080 --> 08:42.275
No, they finish in the shower.

08:42.840 --> 08:45.877
What do you want? I can't help
if I'm not sexually attracted to you.

08:46.040 --> 08:48.076
Yes, you can.
You just have to make an effort.

08:49.560 --> 08:51.755
You know those jokes
you don't get right away?

08:51.920 --> 08:55.833
And then in a day or two,
you find yourself laughing and laughing?

08:56.000 --> 08:57.638
That's me.

08:58.480 --> 09:00.198
I'm one of those jokes.

09:00.880 --> 09:04.759
You'll sleep with me now,
and you'll be attracted to me later.

09:06.200 --> 09:08.270
Please, Sharon, just give me a chance.

09:09.840 --> 09:10.989
Oh, what the hell.

09:14.000 --> 09:15.433
Good to see you, dear.

09:15.600 --> 09:19.275
You look marvelous. For a heroin addict.

09:20.360 --> 09:21.509
Let me ask you something.

09:21.680 --> 09:24.114
If you don't like any of these people,
why do you come?

09:24.280 --> 09:25.998
Charlie, do you read the paper?

09:26.160 --> 09:29.391
Do you have any idea what the Los
Angeles real-estate market is like now?

09:29.560 --> 09:31.437
Can't say I do.
How are those feet feeling?

09:31.600 --> 09:35.593
- You wanna put your shoes back on?
- No one is selling unless they have to.

09:35.760 --> 09:38.638
Which means, I have to be out
working these rooms every night...

09:38.800 --> 09:41.712
...to learn who's getting divorced,
who's dying, can't make bail...

09:41.880 --> 09:43.916
...whose crappy sitcom got canceled.

09:44.080 --> 09:46.958
I mean, let's face it.
I'm not a young woman anymore.

09:47.120 --> 09:50.112
In the old days, I could find out
all that stuff at home on my back.

09:51.840 --> 09:53.114
Evelyn.

09:53.280 --> 09:54.793
Margaret, good to see you.

09:54.960 --> 09:58.157
- How's married life?
- Oh, just one long honeymoon.

09:58.320 --> 10:00.709
That's because she bangs
a different groom every night.

10:02.800 --> 10:05.189
Hi. Charlie Harper.

10:05.680 --> 10:07.989
Oh, my God.

10:08.880 --> 10:10.598
That was amazing.

10:11.360 --> 10:12.475
Wasn't that amazing?

10:12.640 --> 10:14.471
I hate myself.

10:15.760 --> 10:18.479
What? No, no, no, you were great.

10:18.640 --> 10:20.517
You did a crackerjack job.

10:20.680 --> 10:25.515
Why do I always do this? Why do I have
this constant need to degrade myself?

10:28.760 --> 10:30.796
Would it help to cuddle?

10:30.960 --> 10:33.394
Don't touch me.

10:34.000 --> 10:36.195
Okay. No touching.

10:37.000 --> 10:43.109
The image of you lying on top of me
will haunt me forever.

10:46.720 --> 10:48.073
Did you wanna be on top?

10:49.720 --> 10:53.395
Because if you give me a half an hour
and a glass of juice, we can try that.

10:56.480 --> 10:59.472
Hi, hi, Dr. Phillips. It's me, Sharon.

10:59.640 --> 11:01.517
I did it again.

11:01.680 --> 11:03.796
I don't know why.

11:03.960 --> 11:05.075
I felt sorry for him.

11:06.960 --> 11:10.270
Hey, hey, why don't I whip us up
some French toast?

11:11.560 --> 11:13.676
Shut up.

11:14.640 --> 11:19.236
Okay, I'm just gonna get a nice glass
of cran-apple just in case.

11:19.400 --> 11:20.879
How bad was it?

11:21.040 --> 11:23.270
How bad was it? I'm in a fold-out bed.

11:31.000 --> 11:32.115
Morning.

11:32.280 --> 11:33.793
Morning.

11:34.640 --> 11:36.551
Hey, Berta, you're a woman...

11:36.720 --> 11:38.915
Where are we going with this, zippy?

11:39.440 --> 11:40.429
I was just wondering.

11:40.600 --> 11:43.558
What does it mean when someone
starts crying uncontrollably...

11:43.720 --> 11:44.709
...after sex?

11:44.880 --> 11:48.429
Well, in my experience,
it usually means the conjugal visit's over.

11:52.560 --> 11:53.788
Right. Thanks.

11:54.280 --> 11:56.191
What happened?
You get yourself a weeper?

11:56.360 --> 11:57.634
Yeah. Yeah, last night.

11:57.800 --> 11:59.711
I've never seen anything like it before.

11:59.880 --> 12:01.074
That's hard to believe.

12:02.520 --> 12:04.397
I got it.

12:05.240 --> 12:06.753
Hello?

12:06.920 --> 12:08.114
Oh, hey, Mom. How are you?

12:09.000 --> 12:10.558
Yeah, that was fun last night.

12:11.840 --> 12:13.876
No, I'm not doing anything. Why?

12:14.040 --> 12:16.235
Sure. I'd love to go shopping with you.

12:18.240 --> 12:20.390
Great. I'll see you then.

12:26.680 --> 12:28.033
What?

12:28.800 --> 12:30.313
- Nothing.
- Nothing.

12:30.920 --> 12:32.911
Hey, hey, Mom's not that bad.

12:33.080 --> 12:36.390
In fact,
she's kind of fun to hang out with.

12:37.680 --> 12:40.513
That has to be the creepiest thing
I've ever heard.

12:40.680 --> 12:45.356
You know, I said the same thing
to myself just a couple minutes ago.

12:50.760 --> 12:53.638
- You sure you can't stay for dinner?
- Oh, I'd love to, sweetie.

12:53.800 --> 12:57.190
But Teddy's back in town,
and Mommy plans to get laid tonight.

12:57.360 --> 12:59.999
Well, good for you.
Please, give him my best.

13:00.600 --> 13:02.477
Only after I give him my best.

13:04.080 --> 13:06.310
- Hello.
- Oh, hi, Alan.

13:06.480 --> 13:07.959
Don't forget your little gifty.

13:08.120 --> 13:09.519
You bought him a gifty?

13:09.680 --> 13:11.910
My way of saying,
"Thank you for lunch."

13:12.080 --> 13:13.229
You took her to lunch?

13:13.400 --> 13:15.595
I must have gained 5 pounds.

13:15.760 --> 13:17.716
Oh, stop. You have a terrific figure.

13:17.880 --> 13:19.233
Thank you.

13:20.080 --> 13:21.832
Are you high?

13:22.520 --> 13:25.193
It never hurts to pay a compliment
to someone you care about.

13:25.360 --> 13:27.078
Yeah, you should try it
once in a while.

13:27.240 --> 13:29.071
Might cut down
on that postcoital weeping.

13:30.960 --> 13:32.598
How did you know about that?

13:32.760 --> 13:34.637
Berta told me, I told Mom.

13:34.800 --> 13:36.597
Your brother and I
don't have any secrets.

13:39.320 --> 13:41.390
Maybe I'm high.

13:42.160 --> 13:44.151
Okay, well, I must be off.

13:44.320 --> 13:47.790
Places to go, houses to sell,
new widows to cold call.

13:47.960 --> 13:49.439
Oh, oh, that reminds me.

13:49.600 --> 13:52.160
Charlie, some woman named Margaret
called looking for you.

13:52.320 --> 13:53.355
Margaret?

13:53.520 --> 13:55.750
Oh, yeah, Honeymoon Margaret
from last night.

13:55.920 --> 13:57.353
Charlie.

13:57.520 --> 13:59.750
The woman's husband
is one of my biggest clients.

13:59.920 --> 14:03.230
- Oh, Mom.
- Please, I'm not asking as your mother.

14:03.400 --> 14:05.197
I'm asking as your friend.

14:06.920 --> 14:09.309
All right, as a friend, hands off.

14:09.480 --> 14:11.471
Thank you, darling.

14:11.960 --> 14:12.949
I love you.

14:13.120 --> 14:14.553
See you, Alan.

14:15.280 --> 14:17.475
I guess I'll just throw this away.

14:18.640 --> 14:20.437
What?
You're not gonna call her, are you?

14:20.600 --> 14:23.319
Well, it's a bit of a dilemma.

14:23.480 --> 14:25.994
On the one hand,
there's this beautiful, available woman.

14:26.160 --> 14:27.832
- She's married.
- According to Mom...

14:28.000 --> 14:29.149
...not a fanatic about it.

14:30.520 --> 14:34.593
So am I the kind of guy who would go
back on his word to his own mother...

14:34.760 --> 14:36.796
...just for a really hot one-night stand?

14:39.040 --> 14:40.553
Is that a rhetorical question?

14:41.520 --> 14:42.953
Tell you what.

14:43.640 --> 14:44.789
We'll leave it to chance.

14:46.000 --> 14:48.230
If I miss, I'll take the high road.

14:48.400 --> 14:50.197
If it goes in, I'll call Margaret.

15:02.000 --> 15:03.115
I guess it's fate.

15:22.920 --> 15:24.114
Are you ready for me?

15:24.680 --> 15:27.319
Oh, bravo.

15:34.760 --> 15:38.435
Just to be clear,
this is a tit for tat kind of deal, right?

15:38.600 --> 15:40.716
Your husband cheated on you,
the rotten bastard.

15:40.880 --> 15:43.952
- And now you're cheating on him?
- No, he never cheated on me.

15:44.560 --> 15:47.120
Oh, so what?
He's mean to you, he's abusive?

15:47.760 --> 15:49.478
No. He's a doll.

15:51.320 --> 15:52.878
Is he gay?

15:53.040 --> 15:54.951
Not at all.

15:56.080 --> 15:58.435
Was he in some sort
of bizarre hunting accident?

15:59.160 --> 16:00.149
What?

16:00.320 --> 16:03.153
You know, fell crotch-first
into an open bear trap?

16:03.320 --> 16:05.788
No. He's all man.

16:06.400 --> 16:08.436
So then why are you doing this?

16:09.000 --> 16:10.479
Well, it's very simple.

16:10.640 --> 16:13.313
I like having sex with strangers.

16:14.680 --> 16:15.908
Well, good for you.

16:19.280 --> 16:21.510
Is your husband hiding somewhere
watching us?

16:21.680 --> 16:23.113
No. He's in Dallas on business.

16:23.280 --> 16:25.840
Charlie, are we gonna do this or what?

16:26.240 --> 16:29.869
- Actually, I don't think I can.
- Why not?

16:30.040 --> 16:33.874
Well, I kind of promised my mother
I wouldn't.

16:34.040 --> 16:37.032
- Your mother?
- She's also my friend.

16:37.320 --> 16:39.117
So, what do you wanna do?

16:40.800 --> 16:42.074
Tell you what.

16:42.240 --> 16:44.231
We'll leave it to chance.

16:46.000 --> 16:50.039
If I nail this, then, you know, ditto.

16:51.800 --> 16:52.835
Margaret.

16:53.000 --> 16:54.877
- Oh, God.
- Who's that?

16:55.040 --> 16:57.508
- Who do you think?
- Another stranger?

16:57.680 --> 16:58.715
My husband. Get out.

16:58.880 --> 17:00.552
Right.

17:01.640 --> 17:03.790
- Where the hell should I go?
- Out the window.

17:03.960 --> 17:05.552
I'm not going out the window.

17:05.720 --> 17:07.836
- He's an ex-Marine.
- I'm going out the window.

17:13.680 --> 17:15.750
Oh, damn.

17:21.080 --> 17:23.878
- Hi.
- Sharon?

17:24.040 --> 17:26.349
- What's up?
- I was hoping we could talk.

17:26.920 --> 17:28.558
Oh, sure.

17:28.720 --> 17:30.278
May I come in?

17:30.960 --> 17:32.359
- Okay.
- Thanks.

17:32.520 --> 17:34.590
I'm kind of surprised to see you.

17:34.760 --> 17:37.433
I know.
I behaved really badly the other night.

17:38.040 --> 17:39.678
You were a little emotional.

17:39.840 --> 17:42.752
I wasn't a little emotional.
I was borderline psychotic.

17:43.400 --> 17:46.312
Well, since you brought it up,
I'd say you crossed that border...

17:46.480 --> 17:48.948
...with 10 more crazy people
in your trunk.

17:49.560 --> 17:51.152
I know. I'm so sorry.

17:51.320 --> 17:52.514
I get like that sometimes.

17:52.680 --> 17:56.559
It's a combination of low self-esteem,
low blood sugar...

17:56.720 --> 17:59.473
...and mixing red wine
with my dog's painkillers.

18:04.640 --> 18:07.950
I once took my cold medication
with a mimosa.

18:08.120 --> 18:10.111
Spaced me out the whole day.

18:10.560 --> 18:12.312
- So you forgive me?
- Oh, absolutely.

18:12.480 --> 18:14.118
Oh, thank you, Alan.

18:15.320 --> 18:16.878
Don't mention it.

18:22.600 --> 18:23.953
What are we doing?

18:24.120 --> 18:26.031
I'd like to make it up to you.

18:27.240 --> 18:31.074
Do you really think that's a good idea?
Last time it didn't work out so well.

18:31.240 --> 18:33.390
Please, Alan,
just give me another chance?

18:39.760 --> 18:41.478
Oh, what the hell.

18:43.200 --> 18:45.077
- I thought you were in Dallas.
- I was.

18:45.240 --> 18:47.515
I got a phone call telling me
to check on my wife.

18:47.680 --> 18:48.999
A phone call? From who?

18:49.160 --> 18:50.388
That's not important.

18:50.560 --> 18:51.595
This marriage is over.

18:51.760 --> 18:53.113
I want you out of my house.

18:53.280 --> 18:54.315
Well, I'm not leaving.

18:54.480 --> 18:56.471
You're gonna have to,
because I'm selling it.

18:56.640 --> 18:57.993
In this market? Are you crazy?

18:58.160 --> 18:59.275
I've got a great realtor.

18:59.440 --> 19:01.271
And she assures me
she can get top dollar.

19:01.440 --> 19:03.112
You've already talked to a realtor?

19:03.280 --> 19:04.918
Who do you think called me in Dallas?

19:05.080 --> 19:06.513
And she's not just my realtor.

19:06.680 --> 19:08.398
She's my friend.

19:08.560 --> 19:10.516
Oh, Mom.

19:16.120 --> 19:17.189
I hate you.

19:17.360 --> 19:20.113
You're a pig, and you used me.

19:25.160 --> 19:26.479
Hey, she's cute.

19:27.240 --> 19:28.719
Yes, she is.

19:30.560 --> 19:34.314
- So how's it going?
- Well, we're trying to make it work.

19:36.040 --> 19:37.029
Good for you.

19:37.200 --> 19:38.394
So how was your night?

19:38.560 --> 19:40.039
You'd be proud of me.

19:40.200 --> 19:41.997
- I took the high road.
- Congratulations.

19:42.680 --> 19:43.669
Didn't matter.

19:43.840 --> 19:45.637
It rarely does.

19:51.440 --> 19:52.998
Wait a minute. You're telling me...

19:53.160 --> 19:55.515
...Mom knew you were gonna sleep
with that woman...

19:55.680 --> 19:57.830
...and called the husband
so that he'd catch her?

19:58.000 --> 19:58.989
Yep.

19:59.160 --> 20:02.675
The marriage ends and Mom gets
a big commission for selling their house.

20:03.880 --> 20:06.599
She's an evil genius, Alan.

20:07.600 --> 20:11.149
If she lived in Gotham City,
Batman would be toast.

20:12.280 --> 20:15.078
Hey, isn't that your new girlfriend?

20:15.240 --> 20:16.559
Where?

20:16.720 --> 20:18.312
Over there.

20:18.480 --> 20:21.517
Walking into the ocean
with all her clothes on.

20:22.560 --> 20:24.391
Oh, yeah.

20:24.560 --> 20:26.790
She gets a little suicidal
after we have sex.

20:27.840 --> 20:29.193
Yeah, yeah...

20:30.800 --> 20:33.712
Well, I'd better go pull her in.

20:38.000 --> 20:40.230
Ask if she's got a friend.

21:03.920 --> 21:05.911
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

21:06.080 --> 21:08.071
[ENGLISH]
